class.description:
The server passes each joining client's [NetwJoinRequest] to the handler, which may [code]await[/code]. The client is not connected and receives nothing until the handler returns [constant @GlobalScope.OK]. Any other [enum @GlobalScope.Error] refuses it, and the client receives that code unchanged in [signal NetwSession.join_failed], with the reason given to [method NetwJoinRequest.refuse].
[codeblock]
var lobby_open := true

func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_admission(admit)

func admit(request: NetwJoinRequest) -> Error:
    if not lobby_open:
        return request.refuse(ERR_BUSY, "The match has started.")
    return OK
[/codeblock]
Each [NetwAccountProvider] accepted here proves one kind of account before the handler runs.
